# heightfield_terrace

- Label: HeightField Terrace
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 15 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_terrace.html
- Summary (EN): Turns the slopes of a heightfield into stepped plains by quantizing the input height into discrete steps and blending those terraces with the original height. Outputs height, mesa (terrace floors) and cliffs (terrace walls).
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme les pentes d'un champ de hauteur en paliers par quantification en marches, avec sorties height, mesa et cliffs.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the height layer to add terraces to", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Mask", "meaning": "how much of the terraces is mixed with the original height"}, {"name": "Min Height / Max Height (Compute Range)", "meaning": "height band where terraces are created"}, {"name": "Method", "meaning": "Step Size sets each step height directly; Number of Terraces divides the min-to-max range"}, {"name": "Offset", "meaning": "shifts where each step occurs"}, {"name": "Random Step", "meaning": "varies the height added to each level; 0 gives equal steps"}, {"name": "Add Layers / Layers / Seed", "meaning": "adds extra terrace layers with random offsets"}, {"name": "Global Seed", "meaning": "randomizes steps and layers"}]

- Caveats: ["Random Step and Seed only matter when Random Step is non zero or Add Layers is enabled.", "The node outputs height, mesa and cliffs."]

